In .NET MAUI, use the **lifecycle events** API in your `MauiProgram.cs` (or anywhere you configure the app builder):

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // runs when the activity is pausing
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // runs when the activity is stopping
        }));
#elif IOS
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app =>
        {
            // runs when the app enters the background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- Add `using Microsoft.Maui.LifecycleEvents;` at the top.
- Use `#if ANDROID` / `#elif IOS` preprocessor directives to keep platform code separate.
- The handlers give you the native object (`Activity` on Android, `UIApplication` on iOS) so you can call platform APIs directly.
- Other useful events: `OnResume`, `OnDestroy` (Android); `WillEnterForeground`, `WillTerminate` (iOS).
